# Privacy and secrets
- Never read, print, or commit `.env`, `web/.env.local`, or anything in `data/raw/`.
- Never hard-code API keys, client secrets, or tokens. Read them from environment variables.
- Never log access tokens or refresh tokens, even in debug output.
- The browser/web app may only use files from `data/processed/` or `web/public/data/`.
- Strip IP addresses and other identifying fields from anything you output.
- If a change would expose personal listening data publicly in a new way (e.g. a play-by-play log), stop and ask first.
